; Tutorial_6_Explore_Music.inix -- MusicTrail: from an album to the band that made it, to its members, and back; then a genre in rank order.

[about]
Title=6 - Explore Music
Intro=MusicTrail, the greatest albums of ten genres: from an album to the band that recorded it, on to the band's members, and back; an album's article opened; and a genre heard in rank order.
Setup=DbDo is open.
Homework=Pick a genre you love, and follow one album to everyone who made it.

[step]

Say=One want: from an album I know, to the people who made it.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=MusicTrail holds a hundred albums, ten for each of ten genres, and the performers who recorded them.
Key=Alt+Shift+D
Hear=Template Databases dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I choose MusicTrail and press Enter. Albums are in the books' own order: by genre, and within each genre by rank, so the top blues album comes first.
Key=Enter
Hear=Born Under a Bad Sign, Albert King, Blues, Row 1 of 100
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus J, Jump to Record, finds an album by name. I type A Night at the Opera and press Enter.
Key=Control+J
Hear=A Night at the Opera, Queen, Hard Rock, Row 39 of 100
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Shift plus R, Say Related, says what this album leads to, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+R
Hear=performers 1
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Records here are linked through a table of links, called maps, each with a kind: this album was recorded by one performer. Alt plus Right Arrow goes in.
Key=Alt+Right Arrow
Hear=performers: 1 related record
Hear=Queen
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Queen. Shift plus R again.
Key=Shift+R
Hear=albums 1, performers 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The album I came from, and two performers: members of the band. Alt plus Right Arrow, and I choose performers.
Key=Alt+Right Arrow
Hear=performers: 2 related records
Hear=Freddie Mercury
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Down Arrow.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=John Deacon, Row 2 of 2
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Two levels deep. Alt plus Left Arrow comes back one, as a browser goes back.
Key=Alt+Left Arrow
Hear=performers, Queen
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: deep, and not sure how far. Alt plus Home returns to the table I started in, from any depth.
Key=Alt+Home
Hear=albums, A Night at the Opera, Row 39 of 100
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What ties one record to another is its prime, a key DbDo builds from the record itself. Shift plus P, Say Prime, says it.
Key=Shift+P
Hear=A Night at the Opera|Queen
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Every album carries the address of its article. Control plus Shift plus U, Open url, opens it in the browser; Shift plus U says it.
Key=Shift+U
Hear=https colon slash slash en dot wikipedia dot org slash wiki slash A Night at the Opera Queen album
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now a whole genre, in rank. Control plus F, then F for Fields, and I type Vocal Jazz in the genre box.
Key=Enter
Hear=Filter applied. 10 records match.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Home goes to the first. They are already in rank order, since that is how MusicTrail is sorted.
Key=Control+Home
Hear=Ella Fitzgerald Sings the Cole Porter Song Book, Ella Fitzgerald, Vocal Jazz, Row 1 of 10
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Ranked first. A table can also have a window of its own: Control plus Shift plus O, Open Table, opens performers beside the albums.
Key=Control+Shift+O
Hear=Open Table dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter. Shift plus F4 says the windows open, and Control plus Tab moves between them; Control plus F4 closes this one.
Key=Shift+F4
Hear=2 windows: albums, performers
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Say what a record leads to.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus R

[step]

Say=Go into the related records.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Right Arrow

[step]

Say=Come back a level.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Left Arrow

[step]

Say=Return to the start.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Home

[step]

Say=Open the record's web address.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus U
